[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The two salad bowls are centered and framed for a cookbook, presented at a 3/4 overhead 40-degree angle to clearly display the layered ingredients. One bowl is in the sharp foreground, the second slightly blurred behind it. Shallow depth of field with a soft bokeh background. Lighting is soft, natural side light from a window on the left, casting gentle shadows and highlighting the sheen of the lemon-olive oil dressing. Set on an aged, dark oak wood surface with subtle, authentic wear marks. Props include a single wooden spoon resting casually beside the primary bowl, a small discarded garlic skin near the edge, and a few scattered fresh flat-leaf parsley sprigs. Each matte ceramic bowl contains a base of tender, golden-hued cooked bulgur tossed with vibrant red cherry tomato halves, cool green diced English cucumber, and flecks of bright green parsley. The savory, crumbly brown ground beef, seasoned with aromatic cumin and allspice, is piled generously to one side of the bowl, distinct from the vegetable and grain mixture. The dish is finished with a scattering of toasted, crisp sliced almonds on top. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene captures a lived-in, warm, authentic home kitchen atmosphere. Includes slight natural imperfections: an asymmetric garnish placement, a tiny trace of oil on the bowl rim, and a few stray crumbs on the wooden table. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from professional editorial food photography."
]
